\begin{cases}
b - a = 18 \\
-ab = -63
\end{cases}
\] From \(ab = 63\) and \(b = a + 18\), we substitute \(b\) in the equation: \(a(a + 18) = 63\). This simplifies to \(a^2 + 18a - 63 = 0\). Solving this quadratic equation will give us the value of \(a\). \end{think} <answer> 9 </answer>

